<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE January wheat gains A$1.50 per tonne.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE January wheat gains A$1.50 per tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearby January wheat settled A$1.50 higher at A$160.00 a tonne on Wednesday in light trading on the Sydney Futures Exchange.</p>
<p>Traders said two days of declining prices left some with the view that the contract was a bit oversold, encouraging light buying. No other contracts were traded.</p>
<p>Activity was slowing in the run-up to the Christmas holiday and volumes were unlikely to increase much in the next week, one said.</p>
<p>A mixed closing overnight on CBOT injected some uncertainty into the local market, further slowing activity, traders said.  </p>
